<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72508" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνο-θήρας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, a plant <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the root of which smells of wine</i> or <i>was used
				to flavour wine</i> ; but in the best Mss. of <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.19.1
			</span></i> it is <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνοθήρας,</span> as in <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.117
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.89
			</span></i> ; called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνάγρα</span></b> , Gal.l.c., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνόθουρις</span></b>  ibid., <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				15.15
			</span></i> ; cf. <i>onothuris,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				24.167
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
